 561:ARM_SEGGER_RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** /*********************************************************************
 562:ARM_SEGGER_RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *
 563:ARM_SEGGER_RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *       SEGGER_RTT_WriteWithOverwriteNoLock
 564:ARM_SEGGER_RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *
 565:ARM_SEGGER_RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *  Function description
 566:ARM_SEGGER_RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    Stores a specified number of characters in SEGGER RTT
 567:ARM_SEGGER_RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    control block.
 568:ARM_SEGGER_RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    SEGGER_RTT_WriteWithOverwriteNoLock does not lock the application 
 569:ARM_SEGGER_RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    and overwrites data if the data does not fit into the buffer.
 570:ARM_SEGGER_RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *
 571:ARM_SEGGER_RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *  Parameters
 572:ARM_SEGGER_RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    BufferIndex  Index of "Up"-buffer to be used (e.g. 0 for "Terminal").
 573:ARM_SEGGER_RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    pBuffer      Pointer to character array. Does not need to point to a \0 terminated string.
 574:ARM_SEGGER_RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    NumBytes     Number of bytes to be stored in the SEGGER RTT control block.
 575:ARM_SEGGER_RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *
 576:ARM_SEGGER_RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *  Notes
 577:ARM_SEGGER_RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    (1) If there is not enough space in the "Up"-buffer, data is overwritten.
 578:ARM_SEGGER_RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    (2) For performance reasons this function does not call Init()
 579:ARM_SEGGER_RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *        and may only be called after RTT has been initialized.
 580:ARM_SEGGER_RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *        Either by calling SEGGER_RTT_Init() or calling another RTT API function first.
 581:ARM_SEGGER_RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *    (3) Do not use SEGGER_RTT_WriteWithOverwriteNoLock if a J-Link 
 582:ARM_SEGGER_RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** *        connection reads RTT data.
 583:ARM_SEGGER_RTT/SEGGER_RTT.c **** */
